  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on laboratory-scale material testing rather than long-term field deployments under real-world weathering conditions.",
      "what": "This study evaluated the impact of nano-TiO2 on the pore structures, scaling resistance, and freeze-thaw performance of concrete mixtures made with ordinary Portland cement, Class C fly ash, and Grade 100 slag cement. The findings demonstrate that nano-TiO2 significantly enhances frost resistance specifically in fly ash concrete, and the study introduces a simplified indicator to correlate pore system characteristics directly with durability.",
      "why": "It establishes a previously unmeasured synergistic interaction between nano-TiO2 and fly ash, providing a practical method to predict concrete durability and optimize the use of supplementary cementitious materials in cold-weather infrastructure."
    }
